+# Skylark standalone CLI
+
+Build with `npm run build`, then invoke `node dist/cli.mjs` or install this
+package's `skylark` bin. The CLI uses the same `UTOO_PROXY_BIN`,
+`SKYLARK_MCP_URL`, timeout, read retry and SSO configuration as the extension.
+It performs read-only gateway operations. No scheduler or corpus policy lives here.
+
+`skylark listing --url BOOK_URL --output JSON` writes `skylark-listing-1`:
+`complete`, `book` (including book_id/url/items_count), `documents`, `toc`,
+`captured_at`. Each document includes its gateway fields plus string
+`document_id` and `version` (content_updated_at, updated_at, version, or null).
+All listing pages and the TOC must succeed; unique IDs and the advertised count
+must agree, and the count is rechecked after pagination. The gateway has no
+snapshot token, so same-count concurrent remote edits cannot be ruled out.
+No document body is fetched by listing. Failed listing leaves no new output.
+
+`skylark export --request INPUT --output JSON` consumes:
+
+```json
+{"schema":"skylark-export-request-1","documents":[{"document_id":"123","path":"/tmp/123.md","format":"md"}]}
+```
+
+`format: table` or `laketable` uses the native table/columns/records API to
+produce Markdown. Each requested path is atomically published only after its
+complete export succeeds. Empty regular documents receive the extension's
+explicit empty marker; missing/non-string bodies fail. Image URLs use the
+extension's guarded host rewriting, without downloading images. Resource
+preparation and OCR belong to the downstream image tool.
+
+The `skylark-export-result-1` report has `status`, `documents`, and `counts`.
+Each document has document_id/path/status; completed results add actual `version`,
+selected metadata and bytes; failed results add error. Table exports check the
+version before and after record pagination. Callers compare the actual version
+with their selected version. Missing version means unknown, never a fabricated
+successful version. A failed source does not prevent exporting others.
+
+Exit codes: 0 complete, 2 per-document export failures, 1 shared command/storage
+or gateway listing failure, 64 invalid CLI usage. Results go to stdout; progress
+and diagnostics go to stderr. Reports contain paths and metadata, not bodies.
+
+`npm test` runs the existing gateway transport tests and public CLI subprocess
+tests using a local fake proxy; no live gateway, OCR or extraction is called.
